WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
A quiet London suburb at night.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.440
Through the windows:
tiger-skins, a hookah,

3
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.720
a dove-shaped silver lamp.

4
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.910
Wealth from India, carried
home by a retired officer.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.770
Then, in a locked room, a torn
sheet of paper is left on a table.

6
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.150
Four crosses in a line.

7
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.100
Who brought the danger home?

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.860
Does it come from abroad,
or from Britain's own men?

9
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.100
In this mission, you'll
see how empire came home,

10
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.270
as treasure and décor.

11
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:37.070
You'll look at the Rebellion of 1857, and
ask why Small's account of it is one-sided.

12
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.630
And you'll stand at the gate of Agra fort,

13
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.230
as Small hears an offer: "A quarter
of the treasure shall be yours."

14
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.990
Your mission: decide where
the danger really comes from.
